# Manually transcribed by OWID from p. 34: activity rates ('tasa de actividad') for children aged
# 10-14 in Barcelona in 1905, from the city's municipal Censo Obrero. The census distinguishes sexes
# but not precise ages, so the 10-14 rate involves some approximation.
# NOTE: the exact publication for these figures still needs to be confirmed; the citation below is
# provisional.
# In case of updating, upload manually.

# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Activity rates of children in Barcelona, 1905"
    description: |-
      A study of children's work in Catalonia drawing on Barcelona's municipal workers' census (Censo Obrero) of 1905. It reports activity rates for children aged 10-14, for boys and for both sexes together.

      The census distinguishes sexes but not precise ages, so a rate for the 10-14 band involves some approximation. Barcelona is industrial Catalonia rather than Spain as a whole.
    date_published: "1999"

    # Citation
    producer: Borrás Llop
    citation_full: |-
      Borrás Llop, J. M. (1999). Activity rates of children in Barcelona, 1905 (p. 34).

    # Files
    url_main: https://dialnet.unirioja.es/
    date_accessed: '2026-09-06'

    # License
    license:
      name: © Borrás Llop (1999)
